OL,3,GNEWSAAnalysing 500 million calls fell
OL,4,Ato one person, Omagh bomb inquiry hears
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe "painstaking and time-consuming
OL,7,Fwork" of analysing 500 million calls
OL,8,Fconnected to the Omagh bomb fell to one
OL,9,Fperson, a public inquiry has heard.
OL,11,FThe inquiry heard evidence on Wednesday
OL,12,Ffrom a Police Service of Northern
OL,13,FIreland (PSNI) officer, who led its
OL,14,Finquiry team into the bombing until
OL,15,Fearlier this year, and a member of An
OL,16,FGarda Siochana (Irish police).
OL,18,FPSNI Det Ch Insp Pete Billingsley told
OL,19,Fthe inquiry about the volume of calls
OL,20,Fthat had to be analysed in the course
OL,21,Fof the investigation.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
